# ── Database (site + brain share one Postgres DB) ────────────────
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://aiwebsite:aiwebsite@localhost:5432/aiwebsite

# ── Brain (runs locally from packages/brain submodule via PM2) ───
# Since brain v1.89 the API is fail-closed: BRAIN_API_KEYS is REQUIRED
# (comma-separated Bearer keys; the site sends the first one — see
# src/lib/brain-client.ts). Only /twilio/* webhooks are publicly reachable
# (via nginx + Cloudflare tunnel) and those validate Twilio signatures.
BRAIN_API_KEYS=
BRAIN_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3211
BRAIN_PUBLIC_URL=https://ai.xl.net/brain
BRAIN_DB_BACKEND=postgres
BRAIN_POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://aiwebsite:aiwebsite@localhost:5432/aiwebsite
BRAIN_DB_TABLE_PREFIX=brain_
BRAIN_AUDIO_MODE=xai_realtime
# Router v2 staged-rollout flag (brain v1.97, Issue #695): legacy (default,
# behavior-identical) | shadow (compute + log v2 selections, act on legacy) |
# v2 (act on v2 selections for tasks with v2Enabled in the brain's
# data/task-profiles.json). Unset no longer defers the rollout: brain #733
# flipped the default, so unset resolves to v2. Set BRAIN_ROUTER=legacy for
# the one-env-var rollback.
#BRAIN_ROUTER=legacy
# Per-task model pins (brain Issue #729): JSON map {taskName: modelId}, applied
# in selectModelForTask BEFORE the router-v2 hook, so it acts identically under
# EVERY BRAIN_ROUTER mode (this host leaves BRAIN_ROUTER unset, which resolves
# to v2 since brain #733 flipped the default). Entry-level
# validation drops bad pins one-by-one with a `TASK_OVERRIDE_DROPPED` log line
# (unknown task name, kill-switched model, provider key absent — deepseek-ai/*
# needs DEEPINFRA_API_KEY — or no MODEL_PRICING entry); malformed JSON voids
# the WHOLE map. Boot log `TASK_OVERRIDES_ACTIVE {...}` proves the map parsed.
# NOT SET IN PRODUCTION as of 2026-08-07 — this is a prepared template value,
# nothing on this host is pinned to V4 Flash today. The commented value below
# is the DeepSeek V4 Flash exercise if it is ever enabled: the four ephemeral
# cost_critical helper seats only — in-turn summaries, nothing persisted to
# brain_memories, off the visitor latency-critical path. To enable: uncomment
# on the VM .env + restart brain-api; reversal is removing the var again.
#BRAIN_TASK_MODEL_OVERRIDES={"search_summarizer":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","memory_lookup_summarizer":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","older_messages_summarizer":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","counting_synthesis":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash"}
# Dev only: serve canned NDJSON streams from @aicompany/core instead of a real
# brain — lets chat/SMS/email run with no brain process and no OPENAI_API_KEY
# (npm run dev with BRAIN_STUB=1). MUST NOT be set in production; config:check
# fails the boot if it is.
#BRAIN_STUB=1

# ── LLM / voice providers (required for chat + phone) ────────────
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
# Fast first-pass pin (brain v1.90+): REQUIRED for snappy chat. Without it the
# brain's first pass falls back to OPENAI_MODEL (gpt-5-mini, a reasoning
# model) and a simple "Hello" takes 10-50s instead of ~1-2s.
BRAIN_FIRST_PASS_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini
# HF model cache root (brain #725) — default ~/software-brain-data/hf-cache, outside node_modules.
# BRAIN_HF_CACHE_DIR=~/software-brain-data/hf-cache
OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=tts-1
OPENAI_STT_MODEL=whisper-1
XAI_API_KEY=
# Optional providers
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# DeepInfra: 5th brain provider (curated deepseek-ai/* models). Optional today
# — the BRAIN_TASK_MODEL_OVERRIDES V4 Flash pins above are NOT set in
# production, so nothing needs this key yet. It becomes REQUIRED if those pins
# are ever enabled: without it they are dropped (provider_unavailable) and the
# seats fall back silently.
DEEPINFRA_API_KEY=
# Tavily: brain web_search backend AND **required for the blog** — the news
# prefetch (scripts/fetch-ai-news.mjs) and blog.dataSource (src/lib/blog/
# news.ts) both search it; without a key the nightly blog run WARN-skips.
TAVILY_API_KEY=
AA_API_KEY=
# Google AI Studio key for the brain's Gemini planner + google-provider models.
# Unset = brain plans on OpenAI instead (fallback added with brain Issue #684).
GOOGLE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Twilio (Tron Netter voice/SMS number; also sends the /texting
#    phone-verification codes and opt-in confirmations) ───────────
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=
TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=

# Inbound call persona
INBOUND_PHONE_PERSONA_NAME=Tron Netter
INBOUND_PHONE_SITE=ai.xl.net
INBOUND_PHONE_GREETING=Thank you for calling XL.net, this is Tron Netter. How can I help you today?

# ── Email (Resend; domain ai.xl.net must be verified in Resend) ──
RESEND_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM=Tron Netter <Tron.Netter@ai.xl.net>
CONTACT_NOTIFY_EMAIL=ai@xl.net
# Svix signing secret for the inbound-email webhook (/api/webhooks/resend);
# from the Resend dashboard webhook settings.
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Every outbound email is BCC'd here for human oversight (do not remove).
# Defaults to adam@xl.net when unset (src/lib/email/send.ts).
OUTBOUND_BCC_EMAIL=adam@xl.net
# Recipient for the nightly knowledge-refresh report; falls back to
# ADMIN_EMAIL, then adam@xl.net (scripts/refresh-tron-knowledge.mjs).
KNOWLEDGE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# ── OAuth sign-in (see deploy/GOOGLE-OAUTH-SETUP.md) ──────────────
# Google web client "ai.xl.net" in GCP project xl-website-1682362315172.
# Unset = "Continue with Google" shows an unavailable message.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://ai.xl.net/auth/google/callback
# Microsoft Entra app e66a2e8f-c1c1-4b63-9ffe-245db7d5363c.
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_REDIRECT_URI=https://ai.xl.net/auth/microsoft/callback
MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=common
# Comma-separated emails treated as admins by /api/auth/session, the /admin
# pages, and the /api/admin/* routes (src/lib/auth.ts isAdmin()).
# PUBLICATION AUTHORITY (§5.16): a listed address signed in with Google can
# submit an update to a published /work card that goes live on panel pass
# with no second person involved. Adding an address here is a decision to
# grant that, not just admin-page access.
ADMIN_EMAIL=adam@xl.net

# ── Secrets (generate with: openssl rand -hex 32) ─────────────────
SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET=
AUTOMATION_SECRET=
# Auth for middleware→/api/internal/track page-view beacons. UNSET disables
# visit tracking entirely (and /admin/seo + /admin/companies stay empty).
INTERNAL_TRACK_SECRET=

# ── Visitor identification (/admin/companies) ─────────────────────
# MaxMind GeoLite2-ASN database for IP→organization lookups. Gitignored;
# deploy.sh ships it. Defaults to <cwd>/data/GeoLite2-ASN.mmdb.
#MAXMIND_DB_PATH=

# ── Stripe payments (/builders checkout, §5.10) ───────────────────
# Secret API key (sk_live_… / sk_test_…). Without it, POST /api/checkout
# returns 503 and the buy buttons on /builders show a friendly error.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional dashboard-managed Price ID override. When unset, the checkout
# route creates sessions with inline price_data (Cohort $495/mo recurring) —
# no dashboard product setup required.
#STRIPE_PRICE_COHORT=

# ── Ticket Tailor (workshop ticketing) ────────────────────────────
# API key (Box office settings → API), used two ways: from the dev box to
# manage workshop events (ops), and by the site's workshop registration
# alert poller (src/lib/workshop/orders-watch.ts, started from
# instrumentation.ts) which checks for new orders every 5 minutes and
# emails ADMIN_EMAIL. Unset = no polling (the timer logs why and skips);
# /builders links to the public Ticket Tailor event page for checkout.
#TICKETTAILOR_API_KEY=
# Kill switch for ONLY the registration alert emails (unset = enabled).
#WORKSHOP_ORDER_ALERTS_ENABLED=1
# Set to 1 to let the poller run on a dev server / unsupervised checkout
# (local testing); normally only the PM2-supervised checkout polls.
#WORKSHOP_ORDER_ALERTS_FORCE=1

# ── AI Governance builder (/governance, §5.12) ────────────────────
# Kill switch: set to 0 to pause new drafting (creation, research, answers,
# confirm return 503). Reads stay up: project fetches and document downloads
# keep working, and the daily timer keeps running the 30-day retention sweep
# regardless (the deletion promise survives the switch). Unset = enabled.
GOVERNANCE_ENABLED=1
# Global daily Tavily API-call budget for governance domain research
# (~6 calls per fresh domain; the key is shared with the blog + brain
# web_search). At the cap new research parks as "queued" until midnight UTC.
# 300/day = ~600 Tavily credits/day worst case: CONFIRM the Tavily plan
# covers ~18k credits/month before relying on this ceiling. Runtime-
# overridable by the email approval loop (clamped to a 2000 ceiling).
GOVERNANCE_TAVILY_DAILY_CAP=300
# Global daily brain-call budget for governance turns + research distillation.
# JSON mode runs on the full executor model (~$0.10/turn at our budgets), so
# 1500 authorizes roughly $150/day worst case (~$4,500/month if pinned at the
# cap); the AI provider's own billing quota is the true ceiling. Runtime-
# overridable by the email approval loop (clamped to a 5000 ceiling).
GOVERNANCE_BRAIN_DAILY_CAP=1500
# Month-to-date governance Tavily usage that triggers a WARN email from the
# daily timer (soft signal only; set from your Tavily plan's monthly quota).
GOVERNANCE_TAVILY_MONTHLY_WARN=6000

# ── Team work submissions (§5.16) ────────────────────────────────
# Kill switch for the /work/submit intake + editorial panel. Set 0 to stop
# new submissions and panel admission (already-published cards keep
# rendering). Unset = enabled, same semantics as GOVERNANCE_ENABLED.
WORK_SUBMISSIONS_ENABLED=1
# Global daily brain-call budget for the submission panel (work_usage
# ledger). Tripled 2400 -> 7200 on 2026-08-25 (owner directive) in the same
# change that raised the worst case per run from 10 calls to 18: a stage may
# now cost a dispatch plus one recovery dispatch, and a re-attach on a cold
# prompt cache is a second billed generation. A run is admitted only when its
# worst case still fits, so the run cap below is this number divided by that
# worst case: 400 x 18 = 7200. JSON mode runs on the full executor model
# (about $0.10/turn), so 7200 authorizes roughly $720/day worst case; the
# provider's own billing quota is the true ceiling. Unset = the code default
# in src/lib/work/config.ts, which is what production runs. Set this only to
# override, and keep the two numbers consistent if you do.
#WORK_BRAIN_DAILY_CAP=7200
# Global daily panel-run budget (also work_usage). Keep consistent with the
# call cap: runs x brainCallsWorstCasePerRun must not exceed
# WORK_BRAIN_DAILY_CAP. Unset = the code default (400).
#WORK_PANEL_RUNS_DAILY_CAP=400
# On-disk archive store root (src/lib/work/archive-store.ts): every accepted
# upload's durable copy, ledgered in work_archive_files, cleaned only by an
# admin. Unset = data/work-archives under the process cwd, which survives
# deploys (deploy.sh excludes /data/ from rsync) and is gitignored on the
# dev box. Point it elsewhere only at a path the web process can write.
#WORK_ARCHIVE_DIR=/var/www/aiwebsite/data/work-archives
# Queue drain (src/lib/work/queue-drain.ts, started from instrumentation.ts):
# re-kicks queued (received) and deploy-orphaned (stale-running) submissions
# through the same admission gates every 60 s. Set 0 to stop ONLY the
# automation while intake and the manual Retry lever keep working;
# WORK_SUBMISSIONS_ENABLED=0 stops both. Unset = enabled. NOTE: submitter
# copy promises "the review starts automatically", so 0 is an incident
# lever, not a steady state - the queued contract silently reverts to
# press-Retry while it is off. The drain runs only
# in the PM2-supervised checkout (/var/www/aiwebsite); set
# WORK_QUEUE_DRAIN_FORCE=1 to test it from a dev checkout deliberately.
#WORK_QUEUE_DRAIN_ENABLED=1
#WORK_QUEUE_DRAIN_FORCE=1
# Weekly upload-storage report (src/lib/work/storage-report.ts, started from
# instrumentation.ts): mails ADMIN_EMAIL the archive-store usage every Monday
# 14:00 UTC. The last-sent stamp is durable (governance_meta key
# work_storage_report_last_sent) and moves BEFORE the send, so a failed send
# waits a week rather than looping hourly. Set 0 to stop only this email; the
# store, intake and the /admin/work#storage console keep working. Runs only
# in the PM2-supervised checkout (/var/www/aiwebsite); set
# WORK_STORAGE_REPORT_FORCE=1 to test it from a dev checkout deliberately.
#WORK_STORAGE_REPORT_ENABLED=1
#WORK_STORAGE_REPORT_FORCE=1
# Deploy-window gate (src/lib/work/deploy-window.ts, 2026-08-07). Panel
# admission normally refuses only while a deploy still owns the live tree,
# and admits again once that deploy's own cutover has restarted this process,
# so a queued review no longer idles through the post-cutover tail. Set 1 to
# go back to refusing for the WHOLE deploy (the pre-2026-08-07 rule). This is
# the narrow incident lever for that gate: it needs one
# `pm2 restart aiwebsite --update-env` and it leaves intake, the drain and
# the manual Retry lever alone, unlike WORK_SUBMISSIONS_ENABLED=0 (stops
# intake too) or WORK_QUEUE_DRAIN_ENABLED=0 (stops only the timer, so intake
# kicks keep admitting). Unset = the deploy-window behaviour. The admin
# re-run lane always refuses for the whole deploy regardless.
#WORK_DEPLOY_GATE_STRICT=1

# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://ai.xl.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME=XL.net AI
# Optional override for the persona knowledge doc; defaults to
# <cwd>/data/tron-netter-knowledge.md (src/lib/tron-netter/persona.ts).
#TRON_KNOWLEDGE_FILE=

# ── Brain persona defaults (overridden per-request by the site) ───
DEFAULT_BRAIN_NAME=Tron Netter
DEFAULT_PURPOSE=Tron Netter is an AI Agent working for XL.net. He answers questions about XL.net (always saying "we", "us", "our" — he works for XL.net) using only the publicly available content of https://xl.net and https://ai.xl.net. XL.net is a Chicago-based managed IT services provider for small and mid-size businesses. He cannot browse the internet, check weather, or help with unrelated tasks — he politely declines and steers back to XL.net topics.

# ── Build ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manual escape hatch: skips @aicompany/core runtime env validation (and the
# §5.16 queue drain) in instrumentation.ts. Nothing sets it automatically;
# `next build` is already protected by Next's own instrumentation phase
# guard (verified against 16.2.11).
#SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION=1

# ── Deployment (used by deploy/deploy.sh from the dev box) ────────
AIWEBSITE_SSH_IP=
AIWEBSITE_USER=
# Legacy sshpass transport (break-glass only since the 2026-07-12 ssh-key
# switch — deploy.sh requires --allow-sshpass).
AIWEBSITE_PW=
# ssh-key transport (current; see deploy/site-deploy.env): private key path
# on the dev box. Falls back to SSH_KEY_PATH from site-deploy.env
# (~/.ssh/id_ed25519).
#AIWEBSITE_SSH_KEY=

# Stale-bundle detection (§5.12): stamped by the npm build script itself
# (one unix epoch per build, inlined into client AND server bundles). Do
# NOT set this by hand: a manual value without a rebuild makes every open
# tab report itself stale until the next real build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_ID is intentionally NOT set here.

# --- RFP Response (/rfp, ARCHITECTURE.md §5.17) -------------------------
# The section has no env of its own: access is decided in code by
# src/lib/rfp/access.ts (provider must be google AND email domain must be
# exactly xl.net), and its data lives in the shared DATABASE_URL.
#
# It DOES depend on MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID staying honest. That variable is
# "common" today, which means the Microsoft sign-in path accepts any Entra
# tenant on earth and its email claim cannot be trusted. That is why /rfp
# requires a Google session. See §5.17 before relaxing either.

# --- Your AI Roadmap (/roadmap, ARCHITECTURE.md §5.18) ------------------
# Per-client-company portal: domain-keyed workspaces, directory, private
# Your Work lane on the shared /work pipeline, scorecard.
# Kill switch: 0 pauses WRITES (workspace setup, admin requests, Apollo
# import, directory/doc edits, company submissions web + email); reads stay
# up. Unset = on.
ROADMAP_ENABLED=1
# Daily budget slice for the whole CLIENT population on the shared brain
# (roadmap_usage ledger). Company panel runs and title inference draw BOTH
# this and the WORK_* ledger, so heavy client days shrink staff headroom by
# at most this many calls; raise WORK_BRAIN_DAILY_CAP if that bites.
# Raised 600 -> 1200 on 2026-08-25 because admitCompanyRun checks
# WORK_CAPS.brainCallsWorstCasePerRun (now 18) against THIS cap; at 600
# company admission would have fallen from 60 runs a day to 33.
# Unset = the code default (1200).
#ROADMAP_BRAIN_DAILY_CAP=1200
#ROADMAP_PANEL_RUNS_DAILY_CAP=60
# Apollo.io people-search key (host calls the REST API directly for the
# step-2 directory import; the module's outreach sourcing stays disabled and
# does not read this). Missing key = the import button answers "not set up",
# never a boot failure.
APOLLO_API_KEY=your_apollo_api_key_here
# Daily cap on Apollo API page fetches across all companies.
APOLLO_DAILY_CALL_CAP=100
#
# ONE-TIME ENTRA SETUP for verified Microsoft sign-ins (§5.18): in the app
# registration, Token configuration -> add optional claims `email` and
# `xms_edov` to the ID token. Until that is done every Microsoft session is
# roadmap-untrusted (sign-in still works; the portal offers the email-link
# lane instead). MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID stays "common".
